// go.work for local development/testing of the labs/servers/ lab.
//
// This links every standalone Go lab server module (each keeps its own
// go.mod so it still builds/dockerizes independently — see
// labs/servers/README.md) together with the shared trackercollector sink,
// so `go build ./go/admin-backdoor-header/...` (and the other explicit
// module paths) run from labs/servers/ resolve against these modules in one
// shot. It only affects `go` commands run with a working directory inside
// labs/servers/ or below.
//
// Note: `go build ./...` from this directory does NOT recurse into the
// use'd module subdirectories (that's a Go workspace quirk, not a config
// error); build them by explicit path, or `cd` into an individual server
// module and run `go build ./...` there — each go.mod is self-contained.
//
// Deliberately does NOT include the root mega-analyzer module: the root
// module's pkg/ncer/labtest package talks to these lab servers purely over
// HTTP (see pkg/ncer/labtest/helpers.go), never by importing them, so there
// is no compile-time dependency to wire up here — and keeping the root
// module out avoids `go work sync`/`go build` from this directory ever
// touching the root module's go.mod/go.sum.
go 1.26

use (
	./go/admin-backdoor-header
	./go/admin-idor-role
	./go/admin-jwt-none
	./go/path-traversal-download
	./go/sqli-login
	./labkit
	./trackercollector
)
